3
00:01:17,016 --> 00:01:21,783
[Episode 8, Second House]

4
00:01:22,728 --> 00:01:24,428
Mr. Choi!

5
00:01:25,128 --> 00:01:27,872
Mr. Choi, are you alright?
What's wrong with you?

6
00:01:27,872 --> 00:01:29,812
Are we just going to leave him like this?

7
00:01:29,812 --> 00:01:32,016
You're a doctor. Do something!

8
00:01:32,016 --> 00:01:34,432
Right, there are two doctors here!

9
00:01:34,432 --> 00:01:35,708
Wait, wait, hold on!

10
00:01:35,708 --> 00:01:37,692
First, grab something to support his neck.

11
00:01:37,692 --> 00:01:39,628
- Pull yourself together, Joo Bo Sung!
- His neck...

12
00:01:39,628 --> 00:01:42,649
And have him lie flat so he's comfortable.

13
00:01:48,572 --> 00:01:50,348
What do we do? What are we supposed to do?

14
00:01:50,348 --> 00:01:52,980
- We have to get him to the hospital.
- Hospital?

15
00:01:52,980 --> 00:01:55,428
He hit his head after all...

16
00:01:55,428 --> 00:01:57,128
The police!

17
00:01:59,668 --> 00:02:01,656
Let's take a police car.

18
00:02:01,656 --> 00:02:03,084
What did you say?

19
00:02:03,084 --> 00:02:04,851
- T-The police car?
- The police?

20
00:02:04,851 --> 00:02:06,716
You've lost your mind!

21
00:02:07,516 --> 00:02:09,249
That's not a good idea.

22
00:02:17,064 --> 00:02:18,620
Oh, wait...

23
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:21,549
Wait... hold on, just a second...

24
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:31,844
- Hurry, yeah. Hurry.
- Come on.

25
00:02:31,844 --> 00:02:34,392
We're bringing in a patient with head trauma.

26
00:02:34,392 --> 00:02:36,156
Prepare a bed immediately.

27
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:38,049
The door, the door! The door!

28
00:02:38,049 --> 00:02:39,240
- Yeah, get him in, get him in.
- Stop!

29
00:02:39,240 --> 00:02:42,352
We need to get him to the hospital first.
We'll deal with the legal issues later.

30
00:02:42,352 --> 00:02:44,516
What legal issues? You did this!

31
00:02:44,516 --> 00:02:46,883
You piece of trash!
This is all because of you guys!

32
00:02:46,883 --> 00:02:48,816
- Keep it down. Easy, easy.
- Come on, hurry...

33
00:02:48,816 --> 00:02:50,272
What, you're driving, honey?

34
00:02:50,272 --> 00:02:51,516
Of course. It's my car.
Who else would drive it?

35
00:02:51,516 --> 00:02:53,416
Are you going to stay with this punk?

36
00:02:53,416 --> 00:02:55,416
Is that what's important right now?
You go to Ye Ji, quickly.

37
00:02:55,416 --> 00:02:59,040
What are you all doing?
If Mr. Choi dies, it's all your fault!

38
00:02:59,040 --> 00:03:01,220
No.

39
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:04,383
I'll calm Ye Ji down. You go.

40
00:03:04,383 --> 00:03:06,984
I don't know if she'll listen!

41
00:03:06,984 --> 00:03:08,448
Me?

42
00:03:08,448 --> 00:03:09,992
Then should I just let him go by himself?

43
00:03:09,992 --> 00:03:14,083
- No...
- Come on, let's just go!

44
00:03:18,516 --> 00:03:21,248
That's it. Breathe.
You have to keep breathing.

45
00:03:21,248 --> 00:03:22,936
You have to keep breathing.

46
00:03:22,936 --> 00:03:25,083
Darn it.

47
00:03:27,780 --> 00:03:29,308
Seriously...

48
00:03:29,308 --> 00:03:31,920
Why aren't we moving?

49
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:35,992
Oh, for God's sake. What do we do?

50
00:03:35,992 --> 00:03:38,349
Let's put that off until Wednesday.

51
00:03:43,776 --> 00:03:45,476
Ye Ji,

52
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:49,549
can you talk to me for a minute?

53
00:03:53,084 --> 00:03:54,949
Min Seo?

54
00:03:56,216 --> 00:03:58,249
Min Seo, are you there?

55
00:04:01,084 --> 00:04:03,960
Can we talk for a moment?

56
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,849
Sit down here.

57
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:09,049
Just sit for a moment.

58
00:04:15,204 --> 00:04:19,956
Well, about that dead man,

59
00:04:19,956 --> 00:04:22,483
if you know anything, tell me.

60
00:04:25,024 --> 00:04:29,336
I heard you talking
to your friend about it earlier.

61
00:04:29,336 --> 00:04:32,696
Well, it's just that...

62
00:04:32,696 --> 00:04:34,416
We were...

63
00:04:34,416 --> 00:04:37,349
- I mean, I...
- Yeah.

64
00:04:37,349 --> 00:04:38,883
Okay. Take your time.

65
00:04:38,883 --> 00:04:40,983
Well...

66
00:04:40,983 --> 00:04:42,716
I mean, the thing is...

67
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:47,116
Min Seo, are you in there?

68
00:04:47,116 --> 00:04:50,983
Ye Ji, I know you're confused.

69
00:04:51,848 --> 00:04:54,900
I know you don't understand

70
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:58,883
what's happening right now, but...

71
00:04:58,883 --> 00:05:01,504
[My Daughter]

72
00:05:01,504 --> 00:05:03,204
Min Seo!

73
00:05:04,856 --> 00:05:06,556
Ye Ji?

74
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:17,349
Yeah, Ye Ji.

75
00:05:17,349 --> 00:05:18,404
Mom,

76
00:05:18,404 --> 00:05:21,752
that man we saw at the demolition site
knows everything about the accident.

77
00:05:21,752 --> 00:05:24,632
He came looking for us and grabbed Min Seo,

78
00:05:24,632 --> 00:05:27,349
asking her about what happened that day...

79
00:05:27,349 --> 00:05:29,016
<i>Min Seo?</i>

80
00:05:29,016 --> 00:05:30,728
<i>Where are you right now?</i>

81
00:05:30,728 --> 00:05:33,449
Ye Ji? Lim Ye...

82
00:05:40,808 --> 00:05:44,104
Listen, Min Seo's in danger.

83
00:05:44,104 --> 00:05:46,352
- Min... Min Seo? What about her?
- Just now,

84
00:05:46,352 --> 00:05:48,712
Ye Ji just called me,

85
00:05:48,712 --> 00:05:52,212
- saying some man she saw
<i>- The subscriber is not available...</i>

86
00:05:52,212 --> 00:05:54,641
at the demolition site

87
00:05:54,641 --> 00:05:59,616
knows about the accident and has Min Seo.

88
00:05:59,616 --> 00:06:01,712
H-He's got her? What?

89
00:06:01,712 --> 00:06:05,388
Min... Min Seo...
Do you know where Min Seo went?

90
00:06:05,388 --> 00:06:07,088
Min...

91
00:06:07,816 --> 00:06:09,149
[Live tracking:
Min Seo has left the safe zone.]

92
00:06:09,149 --> 00:06:10,349
[Live tracking: 132-43 Ihaeri-gil,
Yongsin-dong, Unpyeong-si, Gyeonggi-do]

93
00:06:10,349 --> 00:06:11,984
Yongsin...

94
00:06:11,984 --> 00:06:15,983
Isn't Yongsin-dong
where your second house is?

95
00:06:17,332 --> 00:06:19,240
That's right.

96
00:06:19,240 --> 00:06:21,016
It's our second house.

97
00:06:30,804 --> 00:06:32,868
Mr. Choi!

98
00:06:32,868 --> 00:06:34,740
Choi...

99
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:36,960
Mr. Choi! Oh, dear.

100
00:06:36,960 --> 00:06:39,524
- No! No!
- What's wrong?

101
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:41,416
He's not breathing!

102
00:06:41,416 --> 00:06:43,520
Hey! Do something!

103
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:47,516
What are we going to do? Oh God, Mr. Choi...

104
00:06:47,516 --> 00:06:51,296
What should I do? Gosh...

105
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:56,416
Someone like me
wouldn't last a day in prison.

106
00:06:56,416 --> 00:06:58,108
No...

107
00:06:58,108 --> 00:07:01,376
I'd lose my medical license too...

108
00:07:02,024 --> 00:07:03,716
Mr. Choi!

109
00:07:03,716 --> 00:07:05,916
Mr. Choi, say something!

110
00:07:06,736 --> 00:07:10,816
This was an accident, right?
It was just an accident...

111
00:07:10,816 --> 00:07:12,220
Mr. Choi! Please say something, Mr. Choi!

112
00:07:12,220 --> 00:07:14,744
Oh, no...

113
00:07:14,744 --> 00:07:16,444
Mr. Choi!

114
00:07:20,783 --> 00:07:24,284
So, you're saying the two of you

115
00:07:24,284 --> 00:07:26,449
weren't together on March 30?

116
00:07:28,192 --> 00:07:29,892
Yeah.

117
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:35,283
But your stories are a little...

118
00:07:39,549 --> 00:07:43,583
your stories are a bit different, though.

119
00:07:47,376 --> 00:07:51,683
Have some tea. It's good for your health.

120
00:07:52,804 --> 00:07:58,749
But from this point on, if you lie,

121
00:07:59,356 --> 00:08:04,883
you might get hurt a little.

122
00:08:28,004 --> 00:08:30,324
Oh, come on.

123
00:08:30,324 --> 00:08:32,083
Sit down.

124
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:55,256
Just because I seem

125
00:08:55,256 --> 00:08:59,604
so kind and friendly, huh?

126
00:08:59,604 --> 00:09:03,228
You must think you can hit me with that.

127
00:09:03,228 --> 00:09:06,383
But I'm not as soft as I look.

128
00:09:14,408 --> 00:09:16,096
[Honey]
Okay, got it.

129
00:09:16,096 --> 00:09:18,096
I'll get there as fast as I can,

130
00:09:18,096 --> 00:09:20,200
and you two, don't ever go in first, okay?

131
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:22,849
Wait until I get there. Understand?

132
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:29,608
What kind of punk took Ye Ji?

133
00:09:29,608 --> 00:09:31,308
Darn it!

134
00:09:38,292 --> 00:09:40,483
He didn't kidnap them, did he?

135
00:09:42,272 --> 00:09:45,324
Then there should at least be
some kind of demand.

136
00:09:45,324 --> 00:09:47,983
But we haven't heard anything yet.

137
00:09:48,856 --> 00:09:53,036
Doesn't this feel a bit too weird? Right?

138
00:09:56,088 --> 00:09:58,388
Ye Ji said it's the man

139
00:09:58,388 --> 00:10:02,183
they saw at the demolition site,

140
00:10:02,183 --> 00:10:04,840
and he knows about the accident.

141
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:09,616
Well, does anything come to mind?

142
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:13,340
- Huh?
- You scared me.

143
00:10:13,340 --> 00:10:17,868
Look, no matter how messed up
things are between the adults,

144
00:10:17,868 --> 00:10:20,808
we need to figure out what's happening,

145
00:10:20,808 --> 00:10:23,172
get our stories straight on what to do
when we get there,

146
00:10:23,172 --> 00:10:25,148
and come up with a plan!

147
00:10:25,148 --> 00:10:26,428
Shouldn't we go save the kids?

148
00:10:26,428 --> 00:10:27,816
Who said we're not going to?

149
00:10:27,816 --> 00:10:31,588
You think you're the only one
worried about the kids? Jeez.

150
00:10:33,016 --> 00:10:34,948
[Cheongnam Jungang 10-ro]

151
00:10:34,948 --> 00:10:38,016
I'll drop you two off up ahead, okay?

152
00:10:40,764 --> 00:10:42,983
This is driving me crazy.

153
00:10:44,940 --> 00:10:49,188
Right, yeah. We'll just delay
reporting the death for a little while.

154
00:10:49,188 --> 00:10:53,683
It's not like taking him to the hospital
right now will bring him back.

155
00:10:54,688 --> 00:10:57,100
Gosh, seriously.

156
00:10:57,100 --> 00:11:00,248
Darn it, what about Ye Ji?

157
00:11:00,248 --> 00:11:02,783
This is driving me crazy!

158
00:11:07,380 --> 00:11:09,316
I'm sorry, Choi Sang Cheol.

159
00:11:18,836 --> 00:11:21,900
So the man holding our kids right now

160
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:26,120
is the twin of the dead man?

161
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:27,456
- Oh, no, what do we do?
- Yeah, yeah.

162
00:11:27,456 --> 00:11:31,992
Wait, is he keeping our kids hostage
to get back at us?

163
00:11:31,992 --> 00:11:33,049
He wouldn't, right?
He wouldn't do that, right?

164
00:11:33,049 --> 00:11:35,868
That's why we need to
call the police right now.

165
00:11:35,868 --> 00:11:39,483
The police can't go into the second house!

166
00:11:39,483 --> 00:11:42,116
I'm asking why not...

167
00:11:44,416 --> 00:11:46,560
Wait...

168
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:49,949
Don't tell me you cleaned up
the mess that day...

169
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,536
Oh, my God.

170
00:11:52,536 --> 00:11:54,944
Oh, god, that...

171
00:11:54,944 --> 00:11:56,255
What should we do?

172
00:11:56,255 --> 00:11:57,744
Exactly.

173
00:11:57,744 --> 00:12:02,783
That's why we need to get there, and fast.

174
00:12:05,449 --> 00:12:10,883
I normally don't hit pregnant women or kids.

175
00:12:16,156 --> 00:12:21,149
Well, who was that man who died?

176
00:12:23,084 --> 00:12:28,436
Well... That man...

177
00:12:28,436 --> 00:12:30,036
I mean...

178
00:12:30,036 --> 00:12:32,049
I mean, I...

179
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,840
Move it!

180
00:12:34,840 --> 00:12:36,552
Move!

181
00:12:36,552 --> 00:12:38,456
I said move!

182
00:12:38,456 --> 00:12:40,072
- Move!
- We're gonna be dead

183
00:12:40,072 --> 00:12:41,532
before we even save the kids.

184
00:12:41,532 --> 00:12:43,036
Oh, jeez.

185
00:12:43,036 --> 00:12:45,984
I always wondered who Min Seo
took after with her terrible driving.

186
00:12:45,984 --> 00:12:47,883
What did you just say?

187
00:12:47,883 --> 00:12:50,316
Min Seo wouldn't have been driving
in the first place

188
00:12:50,316 --> 00:12:52,483
if Ye Ji hadn't talked her into it!

189
00:12:52,483 --> 00:12:54,349
- Talked her into it?
- How did my Min Seo

190
00:12:54,349 --> 00:12:55,983
end up dating a girl like Ye Ji?

191
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:58,936
"A girl like Ye Ji"? "A girl like Ye Ji"?

192
00:12:58,936 --> 00:13:01,049
Ye Ji could've found someone

193
00:13:01,049 --> 00:13:03,856
much prettier and nicer than Min Seo!

194
00:13:03,856 --> 00:13:06,116
- Oh, please!
- God, seriously!

195
00:13:06,783 --> 00:13:09,283
Both Ye Ji and Jae Hong...

196
00:13:09,283 --> 00:13:11,016
- Darn it!
- Oh, my.

197
00:13:11,916 --> 00:13:15,328
You're so... so vulgar.

198
00:13:15,328 --> 00:13:17,476
Jeez.

199
00:13:17,476 --> 00:13:19,016
- You punk, are you crazy?
- It's dangerous, dangerous!

200
00:13:19,016 --> 00:13:22,216
You punk! If we don't take him
to the hospital now,

201
00:13:22,216 --> 00:13:24,249
what kind of suspicion do you think
will fall on me, you punk!

202
00:13:24,249 --> 00:13:25,360
- It's dangerous!
- You punk!

203
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:28,648
You're doing this on purpose because
you think I slept with your wife, huh?

204
00:13:28,648 --> 00:13:31,412
What are you talking about? You crazy psycho!

205
00:13:31,412 --> 00:13:34,696
If we don't go now,
your daughter could die too!

206
00:13:34,696 --> 00:13:36,200
- What?
- Darn it.

207
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,828
Didn't you hear earlier? Huh?

208
00:13:37,828 --> 00:13:40,996
Some lunatic is trying to
kill your daughter too!

209
00:13:40,996 --> 00:13:43,528
What lunatic? Huh?

210
00:13:43,528 --> 00:13:46,116
Then call the police!
Did you call the police? Huh?

211
00:13:46,116 --> 00:13:49,172
Jeez, stop whining about the police already!

212
00:13:49,172 --> 00:13:51,624
That hit-and-run Choi Sang Cheol
mentioned earlier!

213
00:13:51,624 --> 00:13:54,776
It wasn't us. Your daughter
was the one who hit him!

214
00:13:54,776 --> 00:13:55,812
What?

215
00:13:55,812 --> 00:13:59,208
And the guy who's got your daughter
now came looking for revenge!

216
00:13:59,208 --> 00:14:00,408
For God's sake...

217
00:14:00,408 --> 00:14:03,583
You don't know anything,
yet you keep blabbering.

218
00:14:03,583 --> 00:14:06,892
Alright, go ahead and call the police!

219
00:14:06,892 --> 00:14:11,188
Call them and just send your daughter
to prison yourself.

220
00:14:11,188 --> 00:14:13,612
That doesn't make any sense!

221
00:14:13,612 --> 00:14:15,549
Wait, how could my Min Seo...

222
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:17,549
How could Min Seo do that?

223
00:14:17,549 --> 00:14:21,288
Why on earth did Soo Jung
and Kyung Hee fall for a guy like you?

224
00:14:21,288 --> 00:14:23,149
No...

225
00:14:23,149 --> 00:14:25,356
What on earth do they see in you?

226
00:14:25,356 --> 00:14:28,849
Wait, how could she even drive?

227
00:14:57,412 --> 00:15:00,872
I mean, I really didn't know back then.

228
00:15:00,872 --> 00:15:03,348
I genuinely didn't know that man had died.

229
00:15:03,348 --> 00:15:05,564
If we'd gone back...

230
00:15:05,564 --> 00:15:08,748
If we'd gone back,
maybe we could've saved him...

231
00:15:08,748 --> 00:15:11,349
No, we just shouldn't have
had the accident...

232
00:15:11,349 --> 00:15:15,572
Wait, slow down. Okay?

233
00:15:15,572 --> 00:15:17,383
What accident?

234
00:15:20,412 --> 00:15:23,532
I mean, the... the car...

235
00:15:23,532 --> 00:15:25,436
The car... that...

236
00:15:25,436 --> 00:15:26,800
I'm sorry.

237
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:29,016
I mean, I...

238
00:15:29,016 --> 00:15:31,736
was d-driving...

239
00:15:31,736 --> 00:15:35,152
That man got hit by the car.

240
00:15:35,152 --> 00:15:36,852
You're awake?

241
00:15:41,748 --> 00:15:44,616
We only watched.

242
00:15:47,836 --> 00:15:51,416
The reason we were there was...

243
00:15:51,416 --> 00:15:54,649
You saw us there too, feeding the cat.

244
00:15:55,749 --> 00:16:00,249
Then suddenly a car hit that man.

245
00:16:01,364 --> 00:16:04,016
So we were going to report it,

246
00:16:04,964 --> 00:16:08,268
but I got scared and told her
we should just leave.

247
00:16:08,268 --> 00:16:11,116
Oh, you were scared?

248
00:16:16,764 --> 00:16:19,908
The kids. Can you see them?

249
00:16:19,908 --> 00:16:22,864
Then who was the driver?

250
00:16:22,864 --> 00:16:25,183
We couldn't see their face clearly.

251
00:16:26,044 --> 00:16:28,152
It was very dark there...

252
00:16:28,152 --> 00:16:29,912
Dark?

253
00:16:29,912 --> 00:16:33,956
And they were too far away.

254
00:16:33,956 --> 00:16:37,983
No matter how dark

255
00:16:38,992 --> 00:16:41,449
or far away they were,

256
00:16:44,028 --> 00:16:47,083
how could you not recognize
your own mom and dad?

257
00:16:56,068 --> 00:16:59,340
Wait, do you really think this will work?

258
00:16:59,340 --> 00:17:01,283
Just follow the plan.

259
00:17:01,896 --> 00:17:04,312
Don't say anything stupid and ruin this.

260
00:17:04,312 --> 00:17:07,084
Just think about the kids. The kids.

261
00:17:07,084 --> 00:17:08,784
Jeez...

262
00:17:13,048 --> 00:17:15,144
We're so sorry!

263
00:17:15,144 --> 00:17:17,683
We're sorry. We're sorry!

264
00:17:22,427 --> 00:17:25,149
E-Even though it's too late,

265
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:30,876
we'd like to compensate you now.

266
00:17:30,876 --> 00:17:36,056
Of course, no compensation
can ever take away your grief.

267
00:17:36,056 --> 00:17:39,744
We'll... we'll do
whatever you want, anything.

268
00:17:39,744 --> 00:17:43,436
If there's anything you want,
please just tell us.

269
00:17:43,436 --> 00:17:47,383
- Mom, this guy thinks you are...
- Anything I want?

270
00:17:49,276 --> 00:17:51,416
It wasn't my mom. My mom was just...

271
00:17:51,416 --> 00:17:53,412
Wait! Why are you getting so angry?

272
00:17:53,412 --> 00:17:55,783
Wait, I'm sorry. We were wrong.

273
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:58,056
We'll... we'll compensate you for everything.

274
00:17:58,056 --> 00:18:00,296
The kids...

275
00:18:00,296 --> 00:18:04,260
They were so young. It was just an accident

276
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:06,801
they made without knowing better.

277
00:18:06,801 --> 00:18:08,448
The kids?

278
00:18:13,008 --> 00:18:15,052
Which one of the two?

279
00:18:15,052 --> 00:18:17,012
- Huh?
- What?

280
00:18:17,012 --> 00:18:19,016
Well, I mean,

281
00:18:20,048 --> 00:18:23,424
my Ye Ji was just sitting
in the passenger seat.

282
00:18:23,424 --> 00:18:24,932
She wasn't driving.

283
00:18:24,932 --> 00:18:26,756
The driver was M-M-Min...

284
00:18:26,756 --> 00:18:30,552
- M-Min Seo...
- It wasn't my Min Seo! Not my Min Seo!

285
00:18:30,552 --> 00:18:32,264
The car belonged to her family.

286
00:18:32,264 --> 00:18:35,944
- And Ye Ji drove her dad's car...
- Cut the crap!

287
00:18:35,944 --> 00:18:38,716
It was this crazy woman
and her daughter. This was all them.

288
00:18:38,716 --> 00:18:40,328
My kid wasn't even driving.

289
00:18:40,328 --> 00:18:42,820
- She doesn't even know how to drive!
- Jeez. Then... Then...

290
00:18:42,820 --> 00:18:44,383
- why did you clean it up afterward?
- Clean it up? What do you mean?

291
00:18:44,383 --> 00:18:46,192
I have proof. I recorded everything!

292
00:18:46,192 --> 00:18:47,320
- Are you out of your mind?
- I...

293
00:18:47,320 --> 00:18:48,916
- She's completely lost it.
- No, wait a minute.

294
00:18:48,916 --> 00:18:50,583
- Wait!
- Here, look here!

295
00:18:50,583 --> 00:18:53,704
Here. It's right here!

296
00:19:06,416 --> 00:19:09,349
Was that Sol you were carrying?

297
00:19:11,552 --> 00:19:13,008
It was...

298
00:19:13,008 --> 00:19:14,944
It was an accident. Just an accident.

299
00:19:14,944 --> 00:19:16,296
Please...

300
00:19:16,296 --> 00:19:18,683
Please, leave the kids out of this. Please!

301
00:19:18,683 --> 00:19:20,483
Oh, please...

302
00:19:24,228 --> 00:19:26,611
- Mom!
- Ye Ji! Ye Ji!

303
00:19:26,611 --> 00:19:27,664
Mom!

304
00:19:27,664 --> 00:19:30,049
Your... Your brother.

305
00:19:31,052 --> 00:19:33,536
I... I'm the only one

306
00:19:33,536 --> 00:19:36,849
who knows where your brother is.

307
00:19:45,183 --> 00:19:47,849
[Honey, Calling...]

308
00:20:15,908 --> 00:20:19,908
Goodness, why on earth aren't they here yet?

309
00:20:19,908 --> 00:20:21,640
Jeez.

310
00:20:49,724 --> 00:20:51,740
It won't open.

311
00:20:51,740 --> 00:20:53,516
I can't open it.

312
00:20:57,624 --> 00:20:59,516
Get up.

313
00:21:17,236 --> 00:21:18,936
What?

314
00:21:24,228 --> 00:21:25,348
- What? What is it?
- Keep quiet.

315
00:21:25,348 --> 00:21:28,108
- What's wrong?
- Keep it down.

316
00:21:28,108 --> 00:21:29,108
Huh?

317
00:21:29,108 --> 00:21:30,816
Honey!

318
00:21:30,816 --> 00:21:33,168
- Move! I said move!
- Hey, what are you doing?

319
00:21:33,168 --> 00:21:36,316
I'll ram him with the car.
Get out of the way!

320
00:21:54,136 --> 00:21:56,296
Once I give the signal, run far away.

321
00:21:56,296 --> 00:21:57,556
Huh?

322
00:21:57,556 --> 00:21:59,388
Are you out of your mind?

323
00:21:59,388 --> 00:22:01,776
You're gonna get yourself killed.

324
00:22:01,776 --> 00:22:04,349
Either way, once the body turns up,
we're all screwed.

325
00:22:05,420 --> 00:22:08,683
Are you saying there really is
a body under here?

326
00:22:25,283 --> 00:22:27,000
Right now!

327
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:29,048
Right now?

328
00:22:29,048 --> 00:22:30,383
- Move, move, move!
- Hey, hey, what are you doing?

329
00:22:30,383 --> 00:22:31,749
- Are you crazy?
- I said move! Move!

330
00:22:31,749 --> 00:22:33,449
Move out of the way!

331
00:22:35,083 --> 00:22:37,356
[Brake assist
Collision avoidance]

332
00:22:37,356 --> 00:22:39,160
What is this? What's wrong with it?

333
00:22:39,160 --> 00:22:40,849
- Hey, hey, hey!
- Wait a second!

334
00:22:40,849 --> 00:22:42,292
What are we gonna do if it does this now?

335
00:22:42,292 --> 00:22:43,804
Hey! Back up! Back up!

336
00:22:43,804 --> 00:22:45,592
Back up! Darn it!

337
00:22:45,592 --> 00:22:47,292
Back up!

338
00:22:48,208 --> 00:22:50,616
Darn it, what's wrong with this thing?

339
00:22:54,274 --> 00:22:55,908
Stay still!

340
00:22:58,676 --> 00:23:01,783
Oh, sir! Why are you doing this?
Why are you...

341
00:23:04,428 --> 00:23:05,436
Oh, my gosh.

342
00:23:05,436 --> 00:23:07,149
Sir, wait!

343
00:23:13,684 --> 00:23:16,524
I wasn't driving! It was that punk!

344
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:19,000
Calm down. Please, calm down.

345
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:23,084
Hey! You piece of trash!

346
00:23:24,776 --> 00:23:26,704
Min Seo, Min Seo! Girls!

347
00:23:26,704 --> 00:23:28,140
Wait, what...

348
00:23:28,140 --> 00:23:30,532
What are you two doing here? What is this?

349
00:23:30,532 --> 00:23:33,532
Ye Ji, go inside with Min Seo
and lock the door.

350
00:23:33,532 --> 00:23:36,360
You kids get out of here, okay?

351
00:23:36,360 --> 00:23:38,012
What the...

352
00:23:38,012 --> 00:23:39,983
- What are you planning to do with this?
- What else?

353
00:23:39,983 --> 00:23:43,580
Can't you see that man's completely lost it?
Someone's really going to die!

354
00:23:43,580 --> 00:23:45,383
If we're going to die anyway,
we have to do something.

355
00:23:45,383 --> 00:23:47,704
Besides, there are four of us.

356
00:23:47,704 --> 00:23:49,700
Four? You mean "us"? "Us"?

357
00:23:49,700 --> 00:23:52,248
We have two men here now.

358
00:23:52,248 --> 00:23:55,149
Maybe we can still do something.

359
00:23:56,300 --> 00:23:58,796
Oh, dear.

360
00:23:59,572 --> 00:24:02,504
Oh, sir. I'm sorry.

361
00:24:02,504 --> 00:24:05,416
I'm... I'm so sorry.

362
00:24:07,364 --> 00:24:09,064
I'm sorry.

363
00:24:22,688 --> 00:24:23,688
Oh, no!

364
00:24:23,688 --> 00:24:25,920
We have to do something...

365
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:29,616
Oh, my, oh, my...

366
00:24:46,548 --> 00:24:49,144
Who on earth are you people?

367
00:24:49,144 --> 00:24:50,283
- Well...
- Huh?

368
00:24:50,283 --> 00:24:52,984
Well, we're...

369
00:24:52,984 --> 00:24:54,816
We're just nobody.

370
00:24:54,816 --> 00:24:56,249
Then what, was this an accident too?

371
00:24:56,249 --> 00:24:57,549
- Oh, yes, yes.
- Yes.

372
00:24:57,549 --> 00:24:59,812
- That was an accident too.
- Yeah, it was an accident.

373
00:24:59,812 --> 00:25:02,583
I know it's hard to believe, but yes.

374
00:25:08,856 --> 00:25:10,916
Let me ask you something.

375
00:25:11,864 --> 00:25:16,064
Why did you kill Sol
and Choi Sang Cheol? Huh?

376
00:25:16,064 --> 00:25:17,416
Who sent you?

377
00:25:17,416 --> 00:25:19,436
K-Kill them?

378
00:25:19,436 --> 00:25:20,583
Because of him, Choi Sang Cheol...

379
00:25:20,583 --> 00:25:22,716
- Wait, what do you mean by "sent"?
- No, no.

380
00:25:22,716 --> 00:25:25,352
Well, your brother was...

381
00:25:25,352 --> 00:25:27,216
It was an accident caused by Min Seo...

382
00:25:27,216 --> 00:25:28,583
- No, no, no!
- What do you mean, "no"?

383
00:25:28,583 --> 00:25:31,349
- Ye Ji's parents buried Na Sol over there.
- Come on!

384
00:25:31,349 --> 00:25:32,683
What is this woman talking about?

385
00:25:32,683 --> 00:25:34,349
- You punks, darn it.
- She keeps making up weird nonsense.

386
00:25:34,349 --> 00:25:35,692
She really won't stop, jeez.

387
00:25:35,692 --> 00:25:36,988
Alright.

388
00:25:36,988 --> 00:25:38,340
If that's the case,

389
00:25:38,340 --> 00:25:40,816
just die, all of you!

390
00:25:59,649 --> 00:26:01,849
- Dad!
- Oh my god, honey!

391
00:26:01,849 --> 00:26:02,849
- Min Seo!
- Girls!

392
00:26:02,849 --> 00:26:04,616
Ye Ji!

393
00:26:04,616 --> 00:26:06,583
Hey, you punk!

394
00:26:39,444 --> 00:26:41,016
I'm really sorry,

395
00:26:41,016 --> 00:26:43,883
but this is all a misunderstanding.

396
00:26:44,992 --> 00:26:47,116
- Honey!
- Dad!

397
00:26:48,156 --> 00:26:49,856
Ye Ji!

398
00:27:11,888 --> 00:27:14,949
How dare you touch my child!

399
00:28:24,556 --> 00:28:26,256
What the...

400
00:28:50,304 --> 00:28:52,004
This should be enough, right?

401
00:28:52,004 --> 00:28:56,216
Yeah, I got one more bag than last time.

402
00:29:13,856 --> 00:29:15,556
Are you alright?

403
00:29:51,612 --> 00:29:53,312
What do we do?

404
00:29:54,372 --> 00:29:56,700
If we take him to a hospital now...

405
00:29:56,700 --> 00:29:58,616
It'll cause problems...

406
00:30:02,548 --> 00:30:04,248
in many ways.

407
00:30:29,288 --> 00:30:33,188
Still, it's a good thing
we bought plenty of cement.

408
00:30:33,188 --> 00:30:34,983
Right, honey?

409
00:32:52,249 --> 00:32:54,808
[One Month Later]

410
00:32:54,808 --> 00:32:59,404
Yeah. Look into it a little more
and give me a call.

411
00:32:59,404 --> 00:33:01,580
Okay.

412
00:33:01,580 --> 00:33:04,264
Sir, this car is registered
to someone named Na Sol.

413
00:33:04,264 --> 00:33:06,560
- Is it a woman?
- No, a guy.

414
00:33:06,560 --> 00:33:09,188
There hasn't been a theft report for the car,

415
00:33:09,188 --> 00:33:12,716
and his phone has been off ever since,
so they can't track his location.

416
00:33:14,100 --> 00:33:15,800
Sounds like a suspicious death, doesn't it?

417
00:33:16,948 --> 00:33:20,749
Yes, but we'll have to
get the car out first and see.

418
00:33:21,448 --> 00:33:22,964
Why aren't they pulling it out already?

419
00:33:22,964 --> 00:33:25,983
Darn it, when am I going home?

420
00:33:28,172 --> 00:33:31,796
They took the dashcam memory card.

421
00:33:31,796 --> 00:33:33,772
They removed the aftermarket one,

422
00:33:33,772 --> 00:33:35,768
but the factory-installed one is still there.

423
00:33:35,768 --> 00:33:37,140
What factory-installed one?

424
00:33:37,140 --> 00:33:40,728
This is the built-in one,

425
00:33:40,728 --> 00:33:44,116
but the car's old,
so they installed this aftermarket unit.

426
00:33:44,116 --> 00:33:46,396
Still,

427
00:33:46,396 --> 00:33:51,100
we won't know whether the built-in system
recorded anything until we check it.

428
00:33:51,100 --> 00:33:54,992
So if we recover the data,
we might be able to see it?

429
00:33:54,992 --> 00:33:57,049
Yes. We'll have to try.

430
00:33:57,704 --> 00:33:58,948
Sir.

431
00:33:58,948 --> 00:34:01,116
Yeah?

432
00:34:01,116 --> 00:34:03,616
- You know Na Sol, the car owner.
- Yeah.

433
00:34:03,616 --> 00:34:07,804
He's got a twin brother named Na Do.

434
00:34:07,804 --> 00:34:10,628
Apparently they ran
a private investigation agency together.

435
00:34:10,628 --> 00:34:13,116
- A private investigation agency?
- Yeah, but...

436
00:34:13,116 --> 00:34:15,120
it looks like the older brother
is missing too.

437
00:34:15,120 --> 00:34:18,149
There hasn't been any activity
on his phone or cards either.

438
00:34:19,528 --> 00:34:21,649
Both brothers?

439
00:34:23,676 --> 00:34:26,528
Find out their last known locations first.

440
00:34:26,528 --> 00:34:28,649
Last known locations? Okay, got it.

441
00:34:32,524 --> 00:34:33,788
Honey!

442
00:34:33,788 --> 00:34:35,092
Honey, honey, honey!

443
00:34:35,092 --> 00:34:38,524
Honey, did you check this out?

444
00:34:38,524 --> 00:34:40,649
Look at this!

445
00:34:43,108 --> 00:34:46,160
<i>A midsize sedan is being
recovered from a reservoir.</i>

446
00:34:46,160 --> 00:34:47,160
[Vehicle recovered from reservoir,
owner missing for 34 days]

447
00:34:47,160 --> 00:34:48,684
<i>The owner of the vehicle</i>

448
00:34:48,684 --> 00:34:50,672
<i>- has been identified as a PI...</i>
- That's him, right?

449
00:34:50,672 --> 00:34:54,444
<i>He has been missing for 34 days.</i>

450
00:34:54,444 --> 00:34:55,904
<i>- In front of a convenience store</i>
- Yeah.

451
00:34:55,904 --> 00:34:57,812
<i>- at an intersection, Mr. Na was last seen...</i>
- The date matches.

452
00:34:57,812 --> 00:34:59,908
<i>Although the police
launched an investigation,</i>

453
00:34:59,908 --> 00:35:02,740
- A reservoir...
<i>- his whereabouts since then...</i>

454
00:35:02,740 --> 00:35:04,460
What's this about a reservoir?

455
00:35:04,460 --> 00:35:06,736
The police aren't going to

456
00:35:06,736 --> 00:35:10,549
come after us too, are they?

457
00:35:11,180 --> 00:35:14,648
Still, just in case,
should we get our stories straight?

458
00:35:14,648 --> 00:35:16,749
What if the police ask...

459
00:35:17,950 --> 00:35:20,060
What is it?

460
00:35:20,060 --> 00:35:24,016
<i>We're with Cheongnam Police Station.
Could you open the door, please?</i>

461
00:35:25,095 --> 00:35:26,795
<i>Is anyone home?</i>

462
00:35:46,016 --> 00:35:47,783
You really don't remember?

463
00:35:50,032 --> 00:35:51,732
Still?

464
00:35:54,812 --> 00:35:58,249
You were the last ones with Mr. Na Do.

465
00:35:59,049 --> 00:36:01,116
Around 5 p.m. on April 8.

466
00:36:02,620 --> 00:36:05,116
You were staying
at the second house, weren't you?

467
00:36:05,116 --> 00:36:08,249
This is in front of your second house,
Ms. Park Kyung Hee.

468
00:36:14,992 --> 00:36:18,316
You have the right to remain silent,

469
00:36:19,448 --> 00:36:22,568
but if you two keep refusing
to cooperate like this,

470
00:36:22,568 --> 00:36:25,649
I'll have to get a warrant

471
00:36:25,649 --> 00:36:29,316
and start with a search
and seizure of the property.

472
00:36:37,260 --> 00:36:39,349
I'll fill you in on everything.

473
00:36:41,336 --> 00:36:43,816
Yes. You should.

474
00:36:44,976 --> 00:36:46,716
H-Honey...

475
00:36:53,944 --> 00:36:55,644
To be honest...

476
00:37:04,658 --> 00:37:06,358
The truth is...

477
00:37:11,396 --> 00:37:13,096
I...

478
00:37:16,264 --> 00:37:18,116
Mr. Na Do...

479
00:37:25,784 --> 00:37:28,402
was hired by me.

480
00:37:34,360 --> 00:37:36,060
Jae Hong had...

481
00:37:37,040 --> 00:37:39,083
It's Eun Bin's real name.

482
00:37:43,048 --> 00:37:46,456
Jae Hong had an affair
with the woman across the street.

483
00:37:46,456 --> 00:37:48,156
Hold on.

484
00:37:56,283 --> 00:37:57,983
Wait...

485
00:38:04,116 --> 00:38:05,872
What's this?

486
00:38:05,872 --> 00:38:07,572
This...

487
00:38:13,448 --> 00:38:15,249
<i>Mr. Na Do found out that</i>

488
00:38:15,944 --> 00:38:20,776
<i>Jae Hong and the woman
across the street, Ahn Soo Jung,</i>

489
00:38:20,776 --> 00:38:23,416
<i>were heading to the second house.</i>

490
00:38:24,688 --> 00:38:28,483
<i>Mr. Na Do went to
the second house in advance,</i>

491
00:38:52,276 --> 00:38:54,683
<i>and I followed along.</i>

492
00:38:56,583 --> 00:38:59,749
[Ye Ji's Family]

493
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:12,749
Hong!

494
00:39:12,749 --> 00:39:15,249
Hey, Lim Jae Hong!

495
00:39:20,912 --> 00:39:22,612
But...

496
00:39:23,732 --> 00:39:25,689
is Mr. Na Do...

497
00:39:26,822 --> 00:39:28,749
dead?

498
00:39:30,120 --> 00:39:33,056
Why would you think that?

499
00:39:33,056 --> 00:39:38,149
Well, you said I was the last person
to see him, so...

500
00:39:40,720 --> 00:39:45,149
Technically, he's still missing.

501
00:39:48,368 --> 00:39:50,149
Have you ever...

502
00:39:51,592 --> 00:39:54,916
seen this man,

503
00:39:54,916 --> 00:39:59,504
or did Mr. Na Do ever mention
someone named Go Du Sik?

504
00:39:59,504 --> 00:40:01,849
I'm not sure.

505
00:40:03,948 --> 00:40:05,648
But why do you ask?

506
00:40:09,280 --> 00:40:11,216
I told you it wasn't me!

507
00:40:12,696 --> 00:40:15,516
Darn it, why is everyone busting my chops?

508
00:40:15,516 --> 00:40:19,516
We've confirmed evidence
that he was planning to murder Mr. Na Do.

509
00:40:22,432 --> 00:40:25,752
- E-Evidence of a murder?
- M-Murder... murder...

510
00:40:25,752 --> 00:40:27,883
Evidence of a planned murder?

511
00:40:33,344 --> 00:40:34,664
<i>Yes.</i>

512
00:40:34,664 --> 00:40:40,449
<i>On the day of the incident,
Go Du Sik tried to contact Mr. Na Do.</i>

513
00:40:43,316 --> 00:40:47,016
<i>He appears to have followed Mr. Na Do's car.</i>

514
00:40:48,164 --> 00:40:50,749
<i>He deliberately caused the accident.</i>

515
00:40:59,088 --> 00:41:02,816
<i>It looks like he intended to kill Mr. Na Do.</i>

516
00:41:16,236 --> 00:41:17,983
Darn it.

517
00:41:22,955 --> 00:41:26,383
You took care of the car, right?

518
00:41:28,129 --> 00:41:29,829
Yeah.

519
00:41:30,904 --> 00:41:33,149
Where did you put it?

520
00:41:33,149 --> 00:41:35,149
